<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Live: UK PM Andy Burnham faces MPs for first time since taking office</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ff7d7a6f256ad3d28385a2e99457743260d2461b00dd9365fc3d8f3f6339e56</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:21:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-live-uk-pm-andy-burnham-faces-mps-for-first-time-since-taking-office" /><summary type="html">The United Kingdom's new Prime Minister Andy Burnham will face lawmakers in the House of Commons on Tuesday for the first time since taking office six weeks ago. Burnham has promised to deliver renewed national optimism after the downbeat two-year tenure of predecessor Keir Starmer, who announced Tuesday that he would resign his seat in Parliament after 11 years.Watch his speech live on FRANCE 24 at 15:30pm (GMT+2).</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Massive' Russian missile, drone attacks on Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58b7d03e39c6f2e477512e4fc273b47f82ca017a9574f06cac66dca1f6b12d3a</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:50:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-massive-russian-missile-drone-attacks-on-kyiv" /><summary type="html">Russian air attacks killed 12 people and injured several more in Kyiv early on Tuesday, authorities said, in the sixth consecutive day of strikes on the Ukrainian capital. Russia, which began its full-scale invasion of its smaller neighbour in 2022, has escalated its air attacks in recent months, as gains made on the ground have slowed.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia fired over 2,800 drones at Ukraine in August amid war tactic change</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ec635ee548df2136265470ce305e4463a71a05f5806203c5c435af96021e960</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:49:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-fired-over-2-800-drones-at-ukraine-in-august-amid-war-tactic-change" /><summary type="html">Over the course of the month of August, Russia launched more than 2,800 jet-propelled drones at Ukraine, a type of drone that is harder to shoot down. That has come with a massive uptick in the number of drones used, considerind those now found on the frontline are quite a new model: Ukrainian authorities say they are pressed into service almost immediately after leaving the factory. FRANCE 24's Oliver Farry looks at those new drones, and how Russia is using them to try and change the course of the war.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia targets Kyiv and its region for sixth consecutive night of attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1efa3912babea288686f0bedeaacbcabc83f0dde0536af79bb64ad0beeb0efd1</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:39:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-targets-kyiv-and-its-region-for-sixth-consecutive-night-of-attacks" /><summary type="html">At least nine people have been killed and 14 injured in Russian strikes on Ukraine overnight. Moscow targeted Kyiv and the wider region in the attack, hitting a railway depot in the Kyiv. Russia's defence ministry said it had also struck infrastructure in the Southern Odesa region. Russia has intensified strikes on the beleaguered Ukrainian cities in recent weeks disrupting the daily lives of millions of people and triggering up to a dozen air-raid alerts a day.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lake Annecy gun linked to unsolved 2012 murder of British family in French Alps</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:127462655798b2ff5ca67ba132b7798222d69e50876376b70679f49e8bd6110b</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T08:21:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-lake-annecy-gun-linked-to-unsolved-2012-murder-british-iraqi-family-french-alps-chevaline" /><summary type="html">French officials say a Luger pistol fished out from the bottom of Lake Annecy shows similarities to the weapon used in the notorious 2012 killings of a British-Iraqi family and a French cyclist in the nearby village of Chevaline, opening up a new lead in a case that has befuddled investigators for over a decade.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Live: Deadly Russian air attack hits energy and rail infrastructure in Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ec7e2d60fe9687bb5cd0aac09778d5b005685d2ff43f1cf997ad37cd79cdcd9</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T06:04:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-live-deadly-russian-air-attack-hits-railway-depot-in-kyiv" /><summary type="html">Russian ballistic missile strikes apparently targeting energy and railway infrastructure rained down on Kyiv and surrounding areas in the early hours of Tuesday, Ukrainian authorities said, killing at least 12 people. It's the sixth consecutive day of Russian strikes on Ukraine's capital. Follow our liveblog for all the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian missile and drone attack on Kyiv kills at least eight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e271ed8a0cba6b4d6b248c4f3810617079e79296fdd016f5ce0036f82c52153</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T02:26:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-russian-missile-and-drone-attack-on-kyiv-kills-at-least-four" /><summary type="html">A massive Russian missile and drone attack on Kyiv and its surrounding region killed at least eight people and wounded more than a dozen overnight, Ukrainian officials said Tuesday, as children prepared to return to school amid heightened fears of further strikes.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU suspends Brazilian meat imports over antibiotic compliance concerns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df820bd69e486519e51ce3e68e570f420b3193fb7e0188c6241eac790b832137</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T00:14:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-eu-suspends-brazilian-meat-imports-over-antibiotic-compliance-concerns" /><summary type="html">The European Union will suspend imports of Brazilian meat and other animal products from Thursday, citing concerns over Brazil’s compliance with EU rules on antibiotic use in livestock. The move affects poultry, beef, eggs and honey, with Brussels offering no timeline for when trade can resume.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Macron seals €4.3-bn French frigate deal in Sweden</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd43b6a8bc55d28a05ff81fcdb3edd9b2bb77b5067f0d659b9def6a6ff1a3ad5</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T19:28:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-macron-seals-_4-3-bn-french-frigate-deal-in-sweden--14abac052a42.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-macron-seals-%E2%82%AC4-3-bn-french-frigate-deal-in-sweden" /><summary type="html">President Emmanuel Macron on Monday oversaw the signing of a 4.3-billion-euro ($4.9 billon) deal for Sweden to buy four French frigates as France and Sweden seek to tighten cooperation against a backdrop of growing Russian threats. Sweden is racing to boost its defences after Russia invaded Ukraine in 2022, with the Nordic country becoming a NATO member two years later. FRANCE 24's James Vasina reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>As Icelanders say no to resuming EU talks, what issues weighed in the election?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0712fb8672936f8d6ff0d141f55c11ae9665a5beb72483c875798c6164b940ce</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:26:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/as-icelanders-say-no-to-resuming-eu-talks-what-issues-weighed-in-the-election--b151c9c282a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/as-icelanders-say-no-to-resuming-eu-talks-what-issues-weighed-in-the-election" /><summary type="html">Iceland's voters rejected restarting negotiations to join the European Union in a referendum that pitted concerns about geopolitical stability against keeping national control of Iceland’s prized fisheries. Talks with the EU to join the bloc had begun after the 2008 financial crisis but had been ended by a Eurosceptic government. But why did Icelanders say no? FRANCE 24's Armen Georgian tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain blames Israel, Russia for spreading disinformation during Ceuta crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3373c674d101ca02a454db5f272430526253324aa6c47eb9dc6dd9f9377a0ee4</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:24:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-blames-israel-russia-for-spreading-disinformation-during-ceuta-crisis--536350545613.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-blames-israel-russia-for-spreading-disinformation-during-ceuta-crisis" /><summary type="html">Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez said there were signs Russia and Israel had spread the disinformation over Spain's migration policy that triggered last month's rush of migrants into Ceuta, but no evidence of Moroccan ​involvement. Both Israel and Russia have denied their involvement. Over 72,000 migrants ‌irregularly crossed from Morocco into the tiny Spanish territory between July 30 and 31 ⁠in an unprecedented surge. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>In Northern Cyprus, families wait for news of passengers from sunk ferry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0035415474a79b121207207209f6bd9d4a65969b6e2de54fbbe75033f23a6e02</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:04:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/in-northern-cyprus-families-wait-for-news-of-passengers-from-sunk-ferry--efcd34c2b217.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/in-northern-cyprus-families-wait-for-news-of-passengers-from-sunk-ferry" /><summary type="html">Seven people have died after a passenger boat capsized in Northern Cyprus. 267 people were on board and 23 are still missing. The boat capsized just a few miles off Kyrenia Port in northern Cyprus - a territory occupied by Turkey but not internationally recognised. The ferry has now completely sunk - and the company that operates it says it is "deeply saddened by the tragic accident". It says a hotline has been set up to provide passengers' relatives with information.</summary></entry><entry><title>France gears up for an election year defined by a fragmented left</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5c803c026cbbbc1e0ed030fef35b11d5493b96b253149d905855f90d618db9b</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:49:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-gears-up-for-an-election-year-defined-by-a-fragmented-left--3c88d139e4b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-gears-up-for-an-election-year-defined-by-a-fragmented-left" /><summary type="html">It's back-to-school week for France, and its politicians are no exception. With a year set to be dominated by a crucial presidential election, both the left and the right wing are hoping to get candidates that will stand a chance against far-right leader Marine Le Pen, who is currently topping the polls. But for now, the political spectrum remains fragmented. So, who is running so far? FRANCE 24's Clovis Casali tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>France and Sweden look to boost European sovereignty through stronger defence ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c0037509c89dd5434092745e0a4b298a7f05b875f8a7668e068bb1e457076a8</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:22:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-and-sweden-look-to-boost-european-sovereignty-through-stronger-defence-ties--88a1fe36fd43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-and-sweden-look-to-boost-european-sovereignty-through-stronger-defence-ties" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron is visiting Sweden on August 31. The aim of the trip is to strengthen the strategic partnership between the two countries. Boosting defence ties is expected to top the agenda, as the war in Ukraine continues and the threat from Russia persists. The newest member of NATO has also expressed interest in joining France's nuclear deterrence initiative.</summary></entry><entry><title>Police arrest Swiss man after deadly rave shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54a66edd77bc24c4d33b70bc6e7b6b61a8ab0beca671b16d0fd7381e907601b7</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T12:01:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260831-police-arrest-swiss-man-over-after-deadly-rave-shooting--3916a36cf6c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260831-police-arrest-swiss-man-over-after-deadly-rave-shooting" /><summary type="html">Swiss police on Monday said they had arrested a 43-year-old man on suspicion of having carried out a deadly shooting at a rave in the town of Aargau Sunday morning. The attack killed a 22-year-old Italian woman and wounded five other people.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish PM Sanchez says Israel and Russia spread disinformation on Ceuta migrant crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e86ea56f812a3e93805699ee56353c237d605c6eb8136061354e1be4617f428</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T08:20:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260831-spanish-pm-sanchez-says-israel-and-russia-spread-disinformation-on-ceuta-migrant-crisis--3f72af16ac9e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260831-spanish-pm-sanchez-says-israel-and-russia-spread-disinformation-on-ceuta-migrant-crisis" /><summary type="html">Centre-left Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez on Monday alleged that social networks linked to Israel and Russia had spread disinformation about the July migrant crisis in the Spanish exclave of Ceuta. He said the alleged smear campaign, which he maintained had also been magnified by far-right networks, had been driven in part by Madrid's opposition to the wars in Ukraine and the Middle East.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>NATO's Arctic activity poses 'direct threat' to Russia, Lavrov warns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b1062b8a994925332f0c12d6e593d18c4aaa5f72c74672d1b4562084e909ed1</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T02:40:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260831-nato-arctic-activity-direct-threat-russia-lavrov--055328c62902.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260831-nato-arctic-activity-direct-threat-russia-lavrov" /><summary type="html">Russia views NATO’s growing activity in the Arctic as a direct security threat, Foreign Minister Sergei Lavrov said on Monday. NATO launched its Arctic Sentry mission in February to strengthen its presence in the region amid tensions with Moscow and US President Donald Trump’s push to acquire Greenland.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ferry capsizes and sinks off northern Cyprus, killing 8</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f771a9c31606f6a8cc1b6305735c5521d8c084eed730867584ace57da619e785</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T12:08:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-ferry-carrying-more-than-250-passengers-capsizes-off-northern-cyprus--feec88e2674e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-ferry-carrying-more-than-250-passengers-capsizes-off-northern-cyprus" /><summary type="html">At least eight people died when a ferry carrying more than 260 people capsized and sunk off the coast of northern Cyprus on Sunday, according to local authorities. The ship's captain and seven crew members were arrested, said the prime minister of the self-proclaimed Turkish Republic of Northern Cyprus (TRNC).</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Iceland rejects restarting EU accession talks in referendum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce93bb0676ca7f60d05c58c6f6b683669a1f8685de081588f2cdb7de10193104</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:30:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-iceland-rejects-restarting-eu-accession-talks-in-referendum--6c9761c1e20e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-iceland-rejects-restarting-eu-accession-talks-in-referendum" /><summary type="html">Icelanders voted to reject reopening EU membership talks, official results showed Sunday, dealing a blow to the government's push to join the bloc and handing a win to those who argued the country's prized fishing waters were too important to risk. The results will disappoint Brussels, which had hoped to welcome the Nordic country as a new member.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Gunman kills one at Swiss rave party</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:00053326d65d688f7d5a081839ea396034d305062d52618db70f3d90bee90f0d</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:14:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/gunman-kills-one-at-swiss-rave-party--9d00787eff7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/gunman-kills-one-at-swiss-rave-party" /><summary type="html">A large-scale police operation is underway in Switzerland after a shooting at a rave in the town of Aarau, 46 kilometres west of Zurich, left one person dead and five others injured. Swiss daily Blick reported that some attendees initially mistook the gunshots for fireworks, until someone shouted, “everyone down”. Police are appealing to potential witnesses who may have photos or videos of the incident to come forward and share them with investigators. France 24 correspondent John Zarocostas reports from Zurich.</summary></entry><entry><title>Manhunt under way after one killed, multiple injured at Swiss rave</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:daffbf08766c75ffb58c6750679af1a6294cd993db28c6c1e045d6d24be996ca</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T06:52:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-one-killed-five-injured-in-shooting-at-rave-in-switzerland--affc514f1781.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260830-one-killed-five-injured-in-shooting-at-rave-in-switzerland" /><summary type="html">At least one person was killed and five others injured – some seriously – in a shooting at a rave in the northern Swiss city of Aarau, police and local media reported Sunday. A major police operation is underway at the scene, with authorities urging residents to stay away from the area.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Referendum on EU membership: An ‘existential question’ for Icelanders</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d59ffd8737c4922045dbced5ff698eb960132a445841f4ee1ccccbd8ccd7a044</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T12:46:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/referendum-on-eu-membership-an-existential-question-for-icelanders--be87b35411b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/referendum-on-eu-membership-an-existential-question-for-icelanders" /><summary type="html">As Icelanders head to the polls on Saturday to vote in a referendum on whether the country should resume talks with the EU over membership, FRANCE 24 speaks to Eiríkur Bergmann, Professor of Politics at Bifröst University, for more insight into the vote.</summary></entry><entry><title>Warehouse hit by Russian attack stored munitions, Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92e2919de0c4e3aa47c6ac258563586350da0151d0f92099aa3fb0146cfde486</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T12:35:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/warehouse-hit-by-russian-attack-stored-munitions-zelensky-says--67979b139afa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/warehouse-hit-by-russian-attack-stored-munitions-zelensky-says" /><summary type="html">A depot that exploded in a Russian strike overnight was owned by the Ukrainian military and stored shells, drones, and other munitions, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said Saturday. FRANCE 24's Emmanuelle Chaze reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Dozens dead after Russian drone strike hits warehouse</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8460d9fc3f9b6d52a732663a37700b5781822b21310485552d8ea190090bd0b7</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T10:24:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/dozens-dead-after-russian-drone-strike-hits-warehouse--a049a730f3c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/dozens-dead-after-russian-drone-strike-hits-warehouse" /><summary type="html">At least 27 people have died after a Russian drone struck a depot near Kyiv's western suburbs overnight, sparking a huge fire and explosions, authorities said Saturday. FRANCE 24's Emmanuelle Chaze reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iceland votes on whether to resume EU membership negotiations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99e127dcfbd1a173c41b6fb211de76b84f350a98ced63a6b11cbdf07662dfafc</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T08:57:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iceland-votes-on-whether-to-resume-eu-membership-negotiations--31c1b36cac9f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iceland-votes-on-whether-to-resume-eu-membership-negotiations" /><summary type="html">Icelanders go to the polls on Saturday in a referendum on whether to resume membership negotiations with the European Union, in a tight race that will be closely watched in Brussels. The country of just under 400,000 people applied to join the EU in the wake of a 2009 financial crisis that devastated its economy. The membership talks were suspended in 2013 when a eurosceptic government came to power.</summary></entry><entry><title>Hundreds evacuate after Russian strike on depot near Kyiv kills at least 37</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27d24bd8dac754938faa0483a0c2f5f13f15c1f8f810f2a83d4f0be52797cfef</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T08:57:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260829-russian-strike-on-warehouse-near-kyiv-kills-at-least-27-people-hundreds-evacuated--66e26e75e203.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260829-russian-strike-on-warehouse-near-kyiv-kills-at-least-27-people-hundreds-evacuated" /><summary type="html">A Russian drone strike on a depot on the outskirts of Ukraine's capital Kyiv on Friday killed at least 37 people and forced hundreds to evacuate, Ukrainian authorities said Saturday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian strikes hit homes, warehouse, shopping mall across Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb8cc3ac1736d5a4f810f11b25c6750baef93386a235e6c69e4466f1668bd7b8</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T08:51:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russian-strikes-hit-homes-warehouse-shopping-mall-across-ukraine--c7e531cddf21.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russian-strikes-hit-homes-warehouse-shopping-mall-across-ukraine" /><summary type="html">A Russian drone strike triggered a major fire and explosions at a warehouse on the outskirts of Ukraine's capital Kyiv, forcing hundreds to evacuate the region, authorities said early Saturday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Icelanders vote in tight referendum on restarting EU membership talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a66a4602185f27709d07a338566d91b5fdfe0f5a197151ede1600f879dcda2e3</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T06:56:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260829-icelanders-vote-in-referendum-on-whether-to-resume-eu-membership-talks--3f30a61fc087.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260829-icelanders-vote-in-referendum-on-whether-to-resume-eu-membership-talks" /><summary type="html">Iceland will vote Saturday in a tight referendum on whether to reopen membership negotiations with the European Union. Reykjavik applied for EU membership in 2009, following a financial crisis that devastated its economy, but a eurosceptic government suspended the process in 2013.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Norway mourns King Harald as Haakon prepares to take the throne</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e9e8b80818ed6c8c24f63bc7250ac266ba9fc3f762cafae1da6f5fb3c6167d0c</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T16:31:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/norway-mourns-king-harald-as-haakon-prepares-to-take-the-throne--82e23fa26c57.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/norway-mourns-king-harald-as-haakon-prepares-to-take-the-throne" /><summary type="html">Norway is mourning King Harald V after the country's longest-serving monarch died at the age of 89, with tributes pouring in from across Europe. His death paves the way for Crown Prince Haakon to become king, as the royal family faces renewed scrutiny over Crown Princess Mette-Marit's reported past ties to Jeffrey Epstein and the conviction of her son for rape.</summary></entry><entry><title>Greenland to open truth commission over forced contraception scheme</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:747a370f424ae541d6736d698eea1e1d6b4727c9631a7813fec41c0c15209e9c</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T16:05:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260828-greenland-to-open-truth-commission-over-forced-contraception-scheme--4b5e39560116.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260828-greenland-to-open-truth-commission-over-forced-contraception-scheme" /><summary type="html">Greenland's government said Friday it would ⁠establish a Truth and Reconciliation Commission to shed light on a campaign of forced contraception carried out by Danish authorities from the 1960s to 1990, after experts failed to agree on whether the practice constituted genocide. The brutal campaign saw thousands of Indignous women and girls receive intrauterine devices or contraceptive injections without their consent.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
